(OpenAI, 2023b), appear to have acquired a decent ability to generate proper responses to factuality-related queries."},{"id":"c5","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_803bcf846f0092f0","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":5,"quote":"(iii) On BEIR, we use only GPT-4 to re-rank the top-30 passages re-ranked by Chat- GPT."},{"id":"c6","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_06f33e4a99ffa6f0","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":6,"quote":"Method nDCG@1 nDCG@5 nDCG@10 BM25 33.33 45.96 55.77 monoBERT (340M) 78.57 70.65 77.27 monoT5 (220M) 83.33 77.46 81.27 monoT5 (3B) 83.33 78.38 84.62 gpt-3.5-turbo 76.19 74.15 75.71 gpt-4 85.71 87.49 90.45 Table 3: Results on NovelEval."},{"id":"c7","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_18549d59256f78d5","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":9,"quote":"Our experiments on three benchmarks have demonstrated the capability of ChatGPT and GPT-4 in passage re-ranking."},{"id":"c8","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_0e32f47392d44c61","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":12,"quote":"We accessed GPT-3.5-turbo and GPT-4 via the OpenAI API."},{"id":"c9","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_726348a3e5493053","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":5,"quote":"6.2 Results on Benchmarks On benchmarks, we compare ChatGPT and GPT-4 with state-of-the-art supervised and unsupervised passage re-ranking methods."},{"id":"c10","chunkId":"730f1a9f38d16689_c_49909d6a6c4b2105","docId":"730f1a9f38d16689","docTitle":"2404.16130_From_Local_to_Global_A_Graph_RAG_Approach_to_Query_Focused_Summarizati","page":2,"quote":"Results show GraphRAG strongly outperforms vector RAG when using GPT-4 as the LLM."},{"id":"c11","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_e9732f9586d9dbaa","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":5,"quote":"Notably, GPT-4 achieves an average im- provement of 2.7 and 2.3 in nDCG@10 on TREC and BEIR, respectively, compared to monoT5 (3B)."},{"id":"c12","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_b29b11771becd699","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":19,"quote":"As a result, we only utilize GPT-4 for re-ranking the top 30 passages of ChatGPT on BEIR and Mr.TyDi."},{"id":"c13","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_b6a6b4d5ebabe7bc","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":2,"quote":"Figure 1 illustrates that GPT-4 outperforms the previous state-of-the-art models by an average nDCG improvement of 2.7, 2.3, and 2.7 on TREC, BEIR, and My.TyDi, respectively."},{"id":"c14","chunkId":"743155d9b0541c99_c_23d13bb615b14441","docId":"743155d9b0541c99","docTitle":"2401.15391_MultiHop_RAG_Benchmarking_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Multi_Hop","page":2,"quote":"In the second experiment, we assess the reasoning and answering abilities of various state-of-the-art LLMs, including GPT-4, GPT-3.5, PaLM, Claude-2, Llama2-70B, and Mixtral-8x7B, for multi-hop queries when re- trieved text is provided."},{"id":"c15","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_bfa1bb330b9a14be","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":3,"quote":"However, existing methods have limited perfor- mance in re-ranking and heavily rely on the avail- ability of the log probability of model output and thus cannot be applied to the latest LLMs such as GPT-4."},{"id":"c16","chunkId":"743155d9b0541c99_c_84964a89b849aadc","docId":"743155d9b0541c99","docTitle":"2401.15391_MultiHop_RAG_Benchmarking_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Multi_Hop","page":2,"quote":"Using GPT-4 as a data generator, we then take an extensive procedure to construct a diverse set of multi-hop queries, each requiring the retrieval and reasoning over multiple documents."},{"id":"c17","chunkId":"743155d9b0541c99_c_4ac3ba8f211e00d1","docId":"743155d9b0541c99","docTitle":"2401.15391_MultiHop_RAG_Benchmarking_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Multi_Hop","page":8,"quote":"ch that integrates human effort with GPT-4. Additionally, we explore two use cases of MultiHop-RAG in the benchmarking of RAG systems, thereby highlighting the potential applications of this dataset."},{"id":"c18","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_00f29812e30c8e2c","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":19,"quote":"3 Permutation generation 17,370 10 0.347 gpt-3.5-turbo Permutation generation 19,960 10 0.040 gpt-4 Permutation generation 19,890 10 0.596 - rerank top-30 Permutation generation 3,271 1 0.098 Table 11: Average token cost, number API"},{"id":"c19","chunkId":"743155d9b0541c99_c_a191f5bcfece81a2","docId":"743155d9b0541c99","docTitle":"2401.15391_MultiHop_RAG_Benchmarking_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Multi_Hop","page":4,"quote":"Our goal is to use GPT-4 to automatically generate high-quality multi-hop queries using the evidence set. However, the raw evidence obtained from Step 2 is not ideal for query generation due to inconsistency in linguistic structure."},{"id":"c20","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_e2936d52a59d465f","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":18,"quote":"The results indicate that ChatGPT produced 14 duplicate passage identifiers during re-ranking 97 queries on two TREC datasets, whereas text-davinci-003 and GPT-4 did not exhibit any duplicates."},{"id":"c21","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_48bc281c9f001a06","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":4,"quote":"4 Specialization by Permutation Distillation Although ChatGPT and GPT-4 are highly capable, they are also too expensive to deploy in commercial search systems."},{"id":"c22","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_e2cb235211566f42","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":19,"quote":"In terms of average USD cost, GPT-4 is the most expensive, with a cost of $0.596 per query."},{"id":"c23","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_12e8858fc6e24b99","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":18,"quote":"GPT-4 also slightly outperforms ChatGPT in terms of the RBO metric."},{"id":"c24","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_803bcf846f0092f0","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":5,"quote":"Overall, GPT-4 outper- forms the supervised system in most languages, demonstrating an average improvement of 2.65 nDCG over mmarcoCE."},{"id":"c25","chunkId":"730f1a9f38d16689_c_e1febf8730b3e3c0","docId":"730f1a9f38d16689","docTitle":"2404.16130_From_Local_to_Global_A_Graph_RAG_Approach_to_Query_Focused_Summarizati","page":18,"quote":"For example, in a sample dataset (HotPotQA, Yang et al., 2018), GPT-4 extracted almost twice as many entity references when the chunk size was 600 tokens than when it was 2400."},{"id":"c26","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_8c5575d2b1e5625a","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":7,"quote":"(ii) With PG, ChatGPT performs comparably to GPT-4 on nDCG@1, but lags behind it on nDCG@10."},{"id":"c27","chunkId":"d2068edc08df316d_c_fbc468205ecb29c2","docId":"d2068edc08df316d","